  "Question": "Which of the following describes a game that is fair to both players?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "The numbers of participants on both sides are equal",
    "B": "Both players have equal probabilities of winning",
    "C": "Both players have a chance of winning",
    "D": "The game always ends in a draw"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A game is fair when both players have equal probabilities of winning. Merely having a chance of winning does not necessarily make the game fair.",
